59:4. diffs **used (locked) versus published (registry latest)** and reports `current` / `outdated` /
78:therefore never enlarge the published dependency graph or the advisory backlog. Its own dependencies
88:| **REQ-1 Discovery** | The candidate manifest set is derived from `git ls-files` — the set of paths **tracked on `main`** — never from a filesystem walk. |
89:| **REQ-2 Completeness** | Every tracked path whose basename is a recognized manifest or lockfile name is discovered. Nothing tracked is silently missed. |
90:| **REQ-3 Tiering** | Every emitted component carries exactly one tier from the ruled vocabulary `{shipped, dev-tooling, eval-only}`, assigned from a **tracked data file**. |
91:| **REQ-4 Loud gaps** | A tracked manifest with no tier assignment is a **hard error naming the path**. It is never emitted untagged and never silently dropped. |
92:| **REQ-5 Fixture exclusion** | Deliberately fake test-fixture manifests are excluded from the BOM by a **data-driven, auditable** rule — never by a hardcoded special case in code. |
93:| **REQ-6 CycloneDX** | Output is schema-valid **CycloneDX 1.6 JSON**, with a closed `dependencies` graph and a `purl` per component. |
94:| **REQ-7 Resolved versions** | A component's `version` is the **locked/resolved** version, not a manifest range. The declared constraint is preserved alongside it. |
95:| **REQ-8 Direct vs transitive** | Every component is tagged `direct` or `transitive`. LBS §2's triage turns on this distinction. |
96:| **REQ-9 Injectable registry** | The published-version lookup is behind an injectable seam. The test suite **never** requires network. |
