882:| 1 `[P2]` | **CycloneDX validity was self-certified.** `AC-SBOM-10` proved schema validity by calling `sbom_survey.cyclonedx.validate()` — a function from the implementation under test — so a `validate()` returning `None` unconditionally passed while the tool emitted invalid CycloneDX JSON, which is precisely the hand-rolled-SBOM failure the criterion exists to stop. | The oracle is now **independent**: `conftest.independent_cyclonedx_validator()` builds `cyclonedx.validation.json.JsonStrictValidator(SchemaVersion.V1_6)` from the **upstream** library (already a declared dependency, §5.7). A **known-invalid negative control** — `KNOWN_INVALID_CYCLONEDX_DOC`, a component with no `type`, which 1.6 requires — is checked **first**, so an oracle that accepts everything is caught before any clean verdict from it is believed. `sbom_survey.cyclonedx.validate()` survives only as a **cross-check required to agree in both directions**: `None` for the real document *and* a diagnostic for the invalid one, which is the half a stub cannot fake. If the validator distribution is missing, `require_external()` **fails** the criterion naming what to install — it never skips (§5.7). |
